{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/triton-lang/triton/pulls/10888","id":4056804849,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAWaHXs7xze3x","html_url":"https://github.com/triton-lang/triton/pull/10888","diff_url":"https://github.com/triton-lang/triton/pull/10888.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/triton-lang/triton/pull/10888.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/triton-lang/triton/issues/10888","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/triton-lang/triton/pulls/10888/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/triton-lang/triton/pulls/10888/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/triton-lang/triton/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/triton-lang/triton/issues/10888/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/triton-lang/triton/statuses/8bfc4d7adae247b732c2bc09c5f325f067df12bf","number":10888,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"[FRONTEND] Honor `if` filters in list comprehensions","user":{"login":"Hughshine","id":32846078,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyODQ2MDc4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/32846078?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hughshine","html_url":"https://github.com/Hughshine","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hughshine/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hughshine/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hughshine/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hughshine/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hughshine/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hughshine/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hughshine/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hughshine/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hughshine/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Fix #10887.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n`CodeGenerator.visit_ListComp` iterated the comprehension's iterable and appended every element unconditionally, never evaluating the generator's `ifs`. A comprehension with a filter (`[x for x in (...) if cond]`) therefore silently kept the elements the filter should have dropped -- with no error -- diverging from both CPython and `TRITON_INTERPRET=1`.\r\n\r\nEvaluate the `ifs` for each item and append only when all conditions hold. The iterable is a compile-time tuple, so each condition folds to a constexpr bool at trace time and no runtime branch is emitted; an empty `ifs` makes `all(...)` vacuously true, so unfiltered comprehensions are unchanged.\r\n\r\nAdds `test_list_comprehension_if_filter` (parser-only, no device): it fails before this change (the `len(vals) == 2` static_assert trips because all four elements are kept) and passes after.\r\n\r\n# New contributor declaration\r\n- [x] I am not making a trivial change, such as fixing a typo in a comment.\r\n\r\n- [x] I have written a PR description following these\r\n  [rules](https://cbea.ms/git-commit/#why-not-how).\r\n\r\n- [x] I have run `pre-commit run --from-ref origin/main --to-ref HEAD`.\r\n\r\n- Select one of the following.\r\n  - [x] I have added tests.\r\n    - `/test` for `lit` tests\r\n    - `/unittest` for C++ tests\r\n    - `/python/test` for end-to-end tests\r\n\r\n- Select one of the following.\r\n  - [x] I have not added any `lit` tests.","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-07-15T00:34:25Z","updated_at":"2026-07-17T04:14:15Z","closed_at":"2026-07-16T01:15:16Z","merged_at":"2026-07-16T01:15:16Z","merge_commit_sha":"14abad9a7429c81b6337de9d30587ef657cf6955","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[{"login":"ptillet","id":614788,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxNDc4OA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/614788?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ptillet","html_url":"https://github.com/ptillet","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ptillet/f